#
# Similarity-operands counter-example (Don't): a gmeow:SimilarityObservation that carries a
# gmeow:similarityScore (a well-formed dimensionless math:Quantity) but names NEITHER of
# the two vector ROWS it scored — no gmeow:comparesLeftTarget, no gmeow:comparesRightTarget.
# A bare score cannot identify WHICH vector pair produced it, so the proximity is
# unattributable at the operand grain — a similarity result must be grounded to its actual
# operands, not merely to whole projections. It violates the sh:minCount 1
# derived from the gmeow:comparesLeftTarget/gmeow:comparesRightTarget allValuesFrom carriers
# + their class-scoped ClosureEntries (→ shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent), and triggers
# similarity-operands.rq (→ ce:noOperandObs). The observation deliberately carries only the
# operand deficiency: its score is a valid Quantity, so no other requiredness fires.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ce:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/counter-examples/embedding-projection/> .

ce:noOperandScore a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension  math:dimensionless ;
    math:quantityValue "0.90"^^xsd:decimal .

# The score names a magnitude but NO operand rows — the row-level operands are absent.
ce:noOperandObs a gmeow:SimilarityObservation ;
    gmeow:similarityScore ce:noOperandScore ;
    gmeow:queryContext    "nearest neighbours (operand rows unnamed — DON'T)" .
